## Mind-Fitness Activities: Spot-the-Difference and Charades

Not every room in the Interactive Play suite is about physical speed. The mind-fitness activities — including spot-the-difference challenges and Charades — are designed to engage a different kind of attention entirely.

Spot-the-difference at this scale is harder than the paper version. The differences are subtle, the time pressure is real, and doing it in a group means everyone is calling out different answers at once. It's louder and more chaotic than something that sounds calm has any right to be.

Charades in a venue context adds a physical performance dimension that the living room version lacks. You're on your feet, you have a crowd, and the points matter. Groups that include people who aren't interested in running obstacle courses often find these rooms the most engaging part of the session.

The mix of physical and cognitive challenges across the Interactive Play rooms is deliberate. Different people in the group get their moment — which matters when you're planning for 8 or 12 people with different energy levels and interests.

